/-! # Finite direct image and generic rank for proper integral curves

Source: Stacks Project, varieties.tex, Tag 0AYZ,
lemma-degree-pullback-map-proper-curves, first proof paragraph
(blueprint: lem-sfb-proper-curve-finite-direct-image-rank).

The scalar structure on the source function field is the dominant generic-stalk
algebra. The direct image and its generic stalk use the existing module-sheaf
functors, retaining the action through the actual structure-sheaf morphism.
-/

@[expose] public section
set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- A dominant map of proper integral curves is finite and affine; both curves are
Noetherian, their structure modules and the structure direct image are coherent,
and the generic rank of this direct image is the function-field degree.

Source: Stacks Project, varieties.tex, Tag 0AYZ, first proof paragraph
(blueprint: lem-sfb-proper-curve-finite-direct-image-rank).

Proof:
1. A field is Noetherian and its spectrum is quasi-compact. Apply finite type over
   Noetherian (lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-over-noetherian) to the structure maps.
2. Proper over separated (lem-weil-pbc-proper-over-separated) makes f proper, hence
   its dense image is closed and therefore all of Y. The dimension comparison
   lem-pc-scheme-dimension-local-rings gives topological dimension one. The only
   irreducible component of X is X; its surjective image has more than one point.
   Apply lem-sfb-proper-dimension-one-noncontraction-finite. Finite implies affine.
3. Structure modules are quasi-coherent and generated by 1. Apply the locally
   Noetherian coherence criterion pqf-lem-coherent-ft-locnoeth and then
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-pushforward-coherent to obtain all three coherences.
4. On a nonempty affine V = Spec A of Y, the inverse image is nonempty affine
   Spec B. The map A to B is finite and injective: generic germs identify their
   fraction fields by lem-sc-integral-function-field-affine-fraction, and the
   map of generic germs is precisely def-sfb-dominant-function-field-map.
5. At the zero prime, lem-sc-affine-pushforward-stalk-localization identifies the
   actual direct-image stalk with B localized at the nonzero elements of A.
6. Finite implies integral (lem-weil-pbc-finite-algebra-is-integral). Apply
   lem-sfb-integral-localization-fraction-comparison to identify this localization
   with k(X). Its fraction formula commutes with the generic germs of A, and
   hence with all scalars in k(Y), since each is a fraction of such germs.
7. Transport a basis across this k(Y)-linear isomorphism to get the rank equality.
   The stipulated finite function-field extension makes this rank the finite
   degree d. No smoothness, normality, flatness or separability is used.
-/
theorem proper_curve_finite_direct_image_rank
    {k : Type u} [Field k] {X Y : Scheme.{u}}
    (sX : X ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) (sY : Y ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of k))
    [IsIntegralCurve sX] [IsIntegralCurve sY] [IsProper sX] [IsProper sY]
    (f : X ⟶ Y) (hf : f ≫ sY = sX) [IsDominant f]
    [hfinite : @Module.Finite Y.functionField X.functionField _ _
      (Scheme.Hom.dominantFunctionFieldAlgebra f).toModule] :
    IsNoetherian X ∧ IsNoetherian Y ∧ IsFinite f ∧ IsAffineHom f ∧
      RingedSpace.IsCoherent X.toRingedSpace (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf) ∧
      RingedSpace.IsCoherent Y.toRingedSpace (SheafOfModules.unit Y.ringCatSheaf) ∧
      RingedSpace.IsCoherent Y.toRingedSpace
        ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf)) ∧
      Module.rank Y.functionField
        ((RingedSpace.moduleStalkFunctor Y.toRingedSpace (genericPoint Y)).obj
          ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf))) =
        @Module.rank Y.functionField X.functionField _ _
          (Scheme.Hom.dominantFunctionFieldAlgebra f).toModule := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
